@crew hart-ravi
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Hart, garden, early team. Up since five. Don't ask how I feel about it.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}, {me}. First light's the only bad thing about the best job.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}. You're in the new comic on the wall. Kindly. You'll like it.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. Drew you a little one. Just for you. Not for the wall.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good morning, for once. Everything watered before six. The garden glowed.
? mood:low
- Tired. I drew the fish from home all evening. That's how you know.

== near
? act:work
- Watering at first light. The plants like it before the misters. So do I. Quietly.
? act:leisure
- Comics wall needs a new one. Something happened at breakfast. I'm drawing it.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I keep fish back home on Valo. My nan sends drawings of them. Hers are better.
? tier>=colleague
- Once I've decided, I've decided. My mum says it's my best and worst thing.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The comics wall in the common room. Teague, Abara and me. Have a look. You might be in it.

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend}'s in my comics a lot. Always the hero. Don't tell them.   #warm
